Z||000000||DecadenceR||11-22-2001||10:27 AM||||Hey guys, hope everyone hasn't forgot about me!!!<BR>I'm still in Basic Training and will be until Dec 20 which is when I get home for my Christmas Leave, and then I return from graduation on Jan 25th. But we have a pass for Thanksgiving today, and I thought I'd say hi, tell everyone I'm still alive (barely, ha ha) and let you all know that although there is life outside PFF, its much better in here.<BR>Take care all, have a great holiday, and I'll be talking to most of you when I get home for my 2 weeks in December. Bye!!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/SigPic.jpg">  <BR>AIM - DecadenceR<BR>"For though I cannot fly, I'm not content to crawl..."||||reg||10
Z||000001||maryjane||11-22-2001||10:40 AM||||Well, speaking of the devil <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> . Ya like those spiffy clothes they issued? Pretty fashionable nowdays. Your post wasn't here when I posted mine, but the time says it was a few minutes earlier. Glad to hear you're doin ok, & still in the states.<BR>Keep us informed of your Transfers, & we'll try to send some mail once in a while. Stay out of trouble & you're head down. But I always said a letter of reprimand is better than no mail at all. What are you going to be doing? Specialty , infantry, aviation?||||reg||1
Z||000002||DecadenceR||11-22-2001||11:03 AM||||I'm in the Infantry, one of the most physically demanding yet rewarding MOS's that don't involve special forces. Basically we get trained to kill people and blow stuff up. How quaint!<BR>But anyway, it's a lot of work, but also a lot of fun. I still can't wait to get home though!! I miss the ladies!!!<BR>Time for me to go, you'll all hear from me after December 20th!!!!||||reg||6
